BT 1 0 0 1 0 125 Tm 15 TL .12549 .129412 .141176 rg /F2+0 10 Tf 15 TL (Abstract: Commercial dried spaghetti can serve as a substitute when fresh alkaline noodles are difficult to obtain. This) Tj T* (exploratory kitchen trial used a 3 \204 3 design combining baking soda concentrations of 2, 4, and 6 g/L with cooking) Tj T* (times of 10, 12, and 15 minutes. Treatments were assessed for elasticity, smoothness, alkaline aroma, and perceived) Tj T* (similarity to ramen-style noodles, followed by an overall score on a 10-point scale. The highest score, 9.5/10, was) Tj T* (assigned to 4 g/L for 15 minutes, described as golden, springy, smooth, appropriately alkaline, and not noticeably) Tj T* (bitter. The 4 g/L, 12-minute treatment scored 8.5/10 and retained a firmer center. Treatments at 2 g/L produced) Tj T* (limited transformation, whereas prolonged cooking at 6 g/L produced bitterness, astringency, stickiness, and a) Tj T* (soap-like odor. Within the limits of a single-observer exploratory trial, 4 g/L for 15 minutes gave the most favorable) Tj T* (result.) Tj T* ET
